Title: Borrowed Light
Credit: Written by
Author: E2E Revision Fixture
Draft date: Version 1

INT. DETECTIVE OFFICE - NIGHT

The rain streaks the window. VERA sits alone, a Rolex glinting on her wrist as she studies the file.

VERA
Every case leaves a mark. This one left a scar.

She pours coffee from a plain steel carafe. Nothing about the room is remarkable except the silence.

EXT. HARBOR - CONTINUOUS

A Ferrari idles at the pier, engine ticking as it cools. The driver never shows his face.

VERA (V.O.)
He drove like the road owed him something.

INT. ARCHIVE ROOM - LATER

Dusty shelves stretch into the dark. Vera runs a finger along a forgotten ledger and stops.

VERA
Someone wanted this buried. That is reason enough to dig.

INT. STAIRWELL - NIGHT

A single bulb swings overhead. Footsteps echo from somewhere below, unhurried and certain.
